var FT={"Aberrant Spawn":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Aberration mutation: Advantage against charm and mind reading, Psychic resistance, and a tentacle limb that makes 1d6 unarmed strikes.","full":"**Aberrant Mind.** You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the charmed condition on you and against any effect that senses your emotions or reads your thoughts.\n**Psychic Resistance.** You have Resistance to Psychic damage.\n**Tentacle.** One limb is a rubbery tentacle you can use for unarmed strikes. A hit deals 1d6 + your Strength modifier bludgeoning damage.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Psychic"],"notes":[["Note","Aberrant Mind: Advantage on saves against charm and against effects that sense emotions or read thoughts"]]}},"Aquanaut":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Breathe air and water, and swim at your walking Speed.","full":"**Aquatic.** You can breathe air and water.\n**Finned.** You have a swimming Speed equal to your walking Speed.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"mv":{"swim":"speed"}}},"Arachne":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Eight-eyed drow-touched human: Darkvision 120 ft, Poison Spray, then Bane and Spider Climb once each per Long Rest.","full":"**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 120 feet as if bright, and in darkness as if dim. You see only shades of gray in darkness.\n**Spider Magic.** You know the Poison Spray cantrip. At level 3 you can cast Bane once with this trait, and at level 5 Spider Climb once. A Long Rest restores each. You can also cast them with slots of the right level. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma as the spellcasting ability when you take the feat.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Arcane Preparation":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Wizard-style fixed slots: assign a spell to each slot, plus one free bonus slot per level.","full":"Instead of preparing spells, you fix each spell slot to one spell when you finish a Long Rest, picking from spells you could cast with it. A slot can be spent only on its assigned spell, but any slot can be recovered normally. You also gain one bonus slot of each level you have slots for, which has no assigned spell and can cast any spell you know. For example, a level 3 wizard assigns four 1st-level slots and two 2nd-level slots, and also has one bonus 1st-level and one bonus 2nd-level slot that can cast any spell in the spellbook.","pre":"Spellcasting from Cleric, Druid or Wizard. Character creation only"},"Battle Adept":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"One d6 battle die and two maneuvers from the Captain or the Grey Watchman Warden.","full":"You gain one battle die (d6), added to any battle dice you already have. It is spent when used. A short or long rest, or rolling initiative, restores all battle dice.\nYou learn two maneuvers from the Captain class or the Grey Watchman Warden. If a maneuver forces a save, the DC is 8 + your Proficiency Bonus + your Strength or Dexterity modifier.","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Beastman":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Claws for 1d6 slashing unarmed strikes and Advantage on Perception checks to smell.","full":"**Claws.** Your claws make unarmed strikes that deal 1d6 + your Strength modifier slashing damage.\n**Keen Smell.** You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Keen Smell: Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell"]]}},"Bounty Hunter":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Mark a creature for 1 hour to track it, remember every face, and knock out instead of kill.","full":"**Perfect Recall.** You remember the name and face of everyone you have ever met.\n**Mark.** As an action, mark a creature you see within 120 feet for 1 hour. You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks to find it, and you can tell whether it has passed through a place. Only one creature at a time.\n**Bring Them In.** When you reduce a creature to 0 hit points with an attack or spell, you can knock it out instead of killing it.","asi":["WIS"]},"Brutal Grip":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Two-handed damage die with versatile weapons held in one hand, and one-handed use of two-handed weapons at a penalty.","full":"When you wield a versatile weapon in one hand, you can use its two-handed damage die. You can wield a two-handed melee weapon in one hand, treating it as one-handed, but you have Disadvantage on attack rolls made that way.","asi":["STR"]},"Cantrip Specialist":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Learn two of eight Warmage cantrip tricks. Character level counts as warmage level.","full":"You learn two Warmage tricks from this list: Blasting Cantrip, Corrosive Cantrip, Draining Cantrip, Explosive Cantrip, Icy Cantrip, Severe Cantrip, Silent Cantrip, Static Cantrip. Your cantrips count as warmage cantrips for these tricks, and your character level counts as your warmage level where the trick needs it.","pre":"Ability to cast a cantrip"},"Child":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Small size, two fewer skills, Strength and Constitution capped at 16, and two saving throw proficiencies.","full":"You are an adolescent with no place in the dangerous adventuring life. Your size is Small, even if your species is normally Medium. You have two fewer skill proficiencies than other characters of your class. Your Strength and Constitution maximum is 16, not 20. You gain proficiency in two saving throws of your choice.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Chronomancy Initiate":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Chronomancy spells join your list, learn Moment to Think, and four chronomancy spells that never count against your spells.","full":"All spells with the chronomancy tag join your class's spell list if they are of a level your class gets slots for, using your spellcasting ability. You learn the Moment to Think cantrip, which does not count against cantrips known. You learn four chronomancy spells that you cast with this feat. If you prepare spells they are always prepared and do not count against your limit. A wizard adds them to the spellbook at no cost. If you learn spells they do not count against spells known. When you gain a level in your spellcasting class, you can swap one of them for another chronomancy spell of a level you have slots for.","pre":"Spellcasting"},"Dilettante":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"After a Long Rest, spend 10 minutes to gain a weapon, skill or tool proficiency, or a wizard cantrip, until your next Long Rest.","full":"When you finish a Long Rest you can spend 10 minutes practicing. Pick a simple or martial weapon, a skill, a tool, or a wizard cantrip. You gain proficiency with that weapon, skill or tool, or you learn the cantrip and cast it with Intelligence, until you finish a Long Rest."},"Diminutive":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"You are Small, and squeeze through Tiny gaps without penalty.","full":"You were born much smaller than your people, or never grew to full height. You are Small instead of Medium. You take no penalty for squeezing through a space only large enough for a Tiny creature.","pre":"Medium size. Character creation only"},"Downcaster":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Four extra spells of level 3 or lower and the power to split a slot into lower slots.","full":"If you learn spells, you learn four spells of 3rd level or lower from your class list, of levels you have slots for. They do not count against spells known. As an action you can split a spell slot of 5th level or lower into two or more lower slots whose combined level is no more than the original. Slots made this way vanish when you recover slots after a short or long rest.","pre":"Spellcasting"},"Dual-Soul":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Two souls share your body with separate personalities, backgrounds, skills and languages. They swap on odd d20 rolls after a Long Rest.","full":"Two souls fight for control of your body. You keep two sets of personality traits, ideals, bonds and flaws, and the souls have different names. They talk to each other telepathically, but only one controls the body at a time. The other can see through your eyes and hear through your ears. When you finish a Long Rest, roll a d20. On an odd roll, the soul in control switches. Each soul has its own background with different skill and tool proficiencies and different languages. You have only the skills, tools and languages of the soul in control.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Early Riser":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Long rest in 4 hours, short rest in 30 minutes, and regain all Hit Dice on a Long Rest.","full":"A strict routine lets you rest less. You gain the full benefit of a Long Rest in 4 hours and of a Short Rest in 30 minutes. When you finish a Long Rest you regain all expended Hit Dice, not half."},"Elderly":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Pick any number of benefits and an equal number of drawbacks from two tables of old age.","full":"Old age catches up with you, though you are not done adventuring. Choose or roll for any number of benefits from the first table, even none, and the same number of drawbacks from the second.\n**Benefits.** 1: proficiency in History or Insight. 2: proficiency in two sets of artisan's tools. 3: you can always add your Proficiency Bonus to saves against being charmed.\n**Drawbacks.** 1: bad back, your lifting and carrying capacity is halved. 2: forgetful, a roll of 13 on the d20 for an Intelligence check counts as 1. 3: poor eyesight, Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Exotic Mastery":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Proficiency with exotic armor and four exotic weapons of your choice.","full":"You have trained with unusual weapons and armor of irregular design. You gain proficiency with exotic armor and four exotic weapons of your choice.","pre":"Proficiency with martial weapons"},"Favorite Spell":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Pick a spell of 5th level or lower: it casts one level higher with a slot, cannot be counterspelled, and is free once per Long Rest.","full":"Pick a spell you can cast, of 5th level or lower, as your favorite. You can take this feat several times, picking a different spell each time.\nWhen you cast it, you can add a harmless impressive visual effect such as a shower of sparks. When you cast it with a slot, you can treat it as cast with a slot one level higher, up to 9th. It cannot be counterspelled. You can cast it once at its lowest level with no slot, and a Long Rest restores that.","pre":"Spellcasting ability 15 or higher"},"Fickle Fortune":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Track rolls of 10 or lower on the d20. After three in a row, change the next d20 to a 20 (no crit).","full":"Record each time you roll 10 or lower on the d20 for an attack roll, ability check or saving throw. If you roll 10 or lower three or more times in a row, you can change the d20 roll to a 20 right away. If it was an attack roll, it does not score a critical hit."},"Field Commander":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Order an ally to act with a reaction, and deny enemies Advantage against you while two allies are near.","full":"As an action, give an order to an ally within 60 feet that hears you. The ally can use its reaction to take one of these actions: Attack (one attack only), Dash, Disengage, Dodge, Help, Hide, Search or Use an Object.\nWhile you are within 5 feet of two or more allies who are not incapacitated, hostile creatures cannot gain Advantage on attack rolls against you.","asi":["CHA"]},"Firebrand":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Fire-marked human: Fire resistance, Produce Flame, then Burning Hands and Flaming Sphere once each per Long Rest.","full":"**Fire Resistance.** You have Resistance to Fire damage.\n**Flame Magic.** You know the Produce Flame cantrip. At level 3 you can cast Burning Hands once with this trait, and at level 5 Flaming Sphere once, with no material component. A Long Rest restores each. You can also cast them with slots of the right level. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma as the spellcasting ability when you take the feat.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Fire"]}},"Focused Critical":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Pick ranged or melee weapon attacks: they crit on a 19 or 20.","full":"Pick ranged weapon attacks or melee weapon attacks when you take this feat. Attack rolls of that type score a critical hit on a roll of 19 or 20."},"Gambler":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Proficiency with all gaming sets and bet on damage rolls once per turn.","full":"You gain proficiency with all gaming sets and have Advantage on ability checks for games of chance.\nOnce on each of your turns, before you roll damage, you can place a stake on the roll. Pick below the average, or at or above the average. If you guessed right, add one extra damage die. If you guessed wrong, remove the highest damage die."},"Greenskin":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Photosynthetic skin: natural armor 12 + Dex, Advantage against poison, Poison resistance.","full":"**Natural Armor.** Without armor, your base AC is 12 + your Dexterity modifier. You can use it if worn armor would give a lower AC. A shield works as normal.\n**Photosynthetic Resilience.** You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the poisoned condition on you, and Resistance to Poison damage.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Poison"],"notes":[["Note","Natural Armor: with no armor your base AC is 12 + Dexterity modifier"]]}},"Grendel":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Goblinoid-human mix: Small or Medium, Darkvision 60 ft, Fey Ancestry, and bonus on your first combat turn.","full":"**Size.** You are Medium or Small, depending on your heritage.\n**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 60 feet as if bright, and in darkness as if dim. You see only shades of gray in darkness.\n**Fey Ancestry.** You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the charmed condition on you.\n**Grendel Ambition.** On your first turn in combat, you add your Proficiency Bonus to attack rolls, ability checks and saving throws.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Grue":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Shadow-touched human: Darkvision 60 ft and a free reroll of Stealth after being found.","full":"**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 60 feet as if bright, and in darkness as if dim. You see only shades of gray in darkness.\n**Covert.** When you are hidden and a creature finds you with a successful Wisdom (Perception) check, you can reroll your Dexterity (Stealth) check to hide. On a success you silently move and the creature does not notice you. A Short or Long Rest restores it.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Gun-Mage Adept":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Four firearm proficiencies, firearms as focuses, renaissance spells and a finger guns or Concealed Shot cantrip.","full":"You gain proficiency with four simple or martial firearms and can use them as spellcasting focuses. All spells with the renaissance tag join your class's spell list if they are of a level your class gets slots for, using your spellcasting ability. You learn either Concealed Shot or Finger Guns, which does not count against cantrips known. You learn four renaissance spells you cast with this feat. If you prepare spells they are always prepared and do not count against your limit. A wizard adds them to the spellbook at no cost. If you learn spells they do not count against spells known. When you gain a level in your spellcasting class, you can swap one of them for another renaissance spell of a level you have slots for.","pre":"Spellcasting"},"Hexer":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Two witch hexes and Cackle, using Charisma.","full":"You learn two hexes of your choice from the witch class list and gain the Witch's Cackle feature. Use Charisma for the attack rolls and saving throws of these hexes.","pre":"Charisma 13"},"Homebrewer":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Alchemist's supplies and reagent dice equal to your Proficiency Bonus to brew potions of a 3rd-level alchemist.","full":"You gain proficiency with alchemist's supplies if you lack it. Using a set over 10 minutes you can brew potions. You gain reagent dice equal to your Proficiency Bonus and can spend them to brew any potion an alchemist of level 3 can. They lose potency after 24 hours. If you have the alchemist's Reagent feature, you can also spend these dice to add damage to a bomb."},"Hunted":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"+5 passive Perception and instant waking, but 1 in 20 chance a Long Rest is only a Short Rest.","full":"Someone would kill you on sight or drag you to a bad end. The constant paranoia gives you +5 to your passive Wisdom (Perception) and wakes you at once when a creature moves within 30 feet. You rarely sleep soundly. Roll a d20 when you take a Long Rest. On a 1 you get only the benefits of a Short Rest. If you are sure your pursuers are gone for good, such as by leaving the plane or watching your hunter die, you lose this feat.","pre":"Character creation only","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Hunted: +5 passive Wisdom (Perception)"]]}},"Immortal":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Never age, Advantage against disease and poison, Poison resistance.","full":"**Ageless.** You do not age, cannot be aged magically and suffer none of the frailty of old age. You cannot die of old age.\n**Immortal Resilience.** You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end diseases and the poisoned condition, and Resistance to Poison damage.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Poison"]}},"Impaired Vision":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Blinded but with 10 ft blindsight, limited spellcasting by hearing, and immunity to gaze effects.","full":"Injury, illness or birth leaves you unable to see as others do. You rely on hearing and aids such as a white cane. Your condition might range from total blindness to low vision.\nYou have the blinded condition, but attack rolls do not gain Advantage against you because of it. You have blindsight 10 feet. Inside that range you effectively see anything not behind cover, and you see an invisible creature there unless it hides from you.\nYou can cast spells that need you to see a target or area if it is within 30 feet, you have a direct line to it, and you can hear it if it is a creature. Beyond 30 feet you make an ability check with your spellcasting ability against DC 10 + the spell's level. On a success the spell works, otherwise it fails with no effect.\nYou are immune to spells and effects that require you to see, such as a medusa's Petrifying Gaze.\nIf your sight is ever restored, such as by Regenerate, you lose this feat. Talk with your GM about whether that fits your character.","pre":"Character creation only","fx":{"senses":[["Blindsight",10,""]],"notes":[["Note","Impaired Vision: you have the blinded condition. Spells that need sight work only on targets within 30 ft you can reach by a direct line or hear"]]}},"Insectoid":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Antennae give 10 ft blindsight, and lost limbs regrow in 24 hours.","full":"**Blindsight.** Your antennae give you blindsight 10 feet. Within it you effectively see anything not behind cover, even blinded or in darkness, and you see invisible creatures unless they hide.\n**Regenerative.** If a body part is amputated without killing you, you regrow it fully in 24 hours.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"senses":[["Blindsight",10,""]]}},"Iron Hero":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"+2 AC against higher-CR attackers, Advantage against whoever downed an ally, and cancel a legendary action.","full":"When a creature with a Challenge Rating higher than your level attacks you, you have +2 AC. You have Advantage on attack rolls against any creature that reduced one of your allies to 0 hit points in the last round. When a hostile creature you see takes a legendary action, you can use your reaction to intercede and stop it. A Short or Long Rest restores that."},"Jinxed":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Pick a number from 2 to 19. When you or an attacker against you rolls it on the d20, it becomes a 1.","full":"You were born under a bad star or struck by a hex that damaged your luck. Pick a number from 2 to 19. When you roll that number on an ability check or attack roll, the d20 becomes a 1. When a creature rolls that number on an attack against you or on a contested ability check against you, its d20 also becomes a 1.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Lower Limb Disability":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Needs a mobility aid, cannot Dash on difficult terrain, Advantage against being knocked prone or moved.","full":"Injury, illness or birth means you cannot walk as others do and rely on an aid for mobility, such as crutches, a wheelchair, or a mechanical or magical support. Work with the GM on what fits the setting.\nYou cannot take the Dash action on difficult terrain. You have Advantage on ability checks and saves made to avoid being knocked prone or moved against your will.\nIf your mobility is ever restored, such as by Regenerate, you lose this feat. Talk with your GM about whether that fits your character.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Marksman's Luck":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Once per turn, flip one ranged weapon damage die (not a d4) to its opposite face.","full":"Once per turn, when you roll damage with a ranged weapon, you can flip one damage die and use the number on its underside instead. This does not work on d4s. The opposite faces of a fair die add up to one more than its highest number."},"Master Thrower":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Bonus action thrown attack, free weapon draws, and doubled thrown ranges.","full":"When you take the Attack action, you can use a bonus action to make a ranged attack with a thrown weapon. You do not add your ability modifier to its damage unless the modifier is negative. When you make a ranged weapon attack you can draw the weapon as part of it, and you can draw any number of weapons this way each round. Short and long ranges of your thrown weapons double.","pre":"Dexterity 13","asi":["DEX"]},"Mul":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Human-dwarf blood: Darkvision 60 ft, heavy armor without penalties, and 1 extra hit point per level.","full":"**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 60 feet as if bright, and in darkness as if dim. You see only shades of gray in darkness.\n**Armor Acclimation.** Heavy armor never lowers your Speed and never gives you Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks.\n**Dwarven Toughness.** Your hit point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 more each time you gain a level.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"senses":[["Darkvision",60,""]],"notes":[["Note","Dwarven Toughness: +1 hit point maximum, and +1 per level"]]}},"Ogre-Blooded":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Darkvision 60 ft, Athletics proficiency with a floor on your checks, and Powerful Build.","full":"**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 60 feet as if bright, and in darkness as if dim. You see only shades of gray in darkness.\n**Monstrous Strength.** You gain proficiency in Athletics. On a Strength (Athletics) check you can treat the d20 result as 10 or as your level plus your Strength modifier, whichever is higher.\n**Powerful Build.** You count as one size larger for carrying capacity and for the weight you can push, drag or lift.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"senses":[["Darkvision",60,""]],"skills":["Athletics"]}},"Owlbearman":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Beak for 1d6 piercing unarmed strikes, and grapple creatures two sizes larger.","full":"**Beak.** Your hooked beak makes unarmed strikes that deal 1d6 + your Strength modifier piercing damage.\n**Owlbear Wrestling.** You can grapple creatures up to two sizes larger than you. You have Advantage on grapple checks on your turn against creatures at least one size smaller than you.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Porterling":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Escape grapples and bindings with Advantage, add d8 feet to jumps, and squeeze through tight spaces.","full":"**Flexible.** You have Advantage on checks to escape a grapple or slip out of bindings.\n**Springheel Leap.** When you make a long or high jump, roll a d8 and add it to the feet you cover, even from a standing jump. The extra distance costs movement as usual.\n**Squeeze.** You take no penalty for squeezing through a space made for a creature one size smaller than you.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Precognitive":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Three times per Long Rest, roll a d20 at turn start and use it for your next attack, check or save this turn.","full":"You sense events an instant before they happen. When your turn begins, you can roll a d20 and note the number. The next attack roll, ability check or saving throw you make before the end of the turn uses this number in place of the roll. You can do this three times, and a Long Rest restores all uses.","pre":"Wisdom 13","asi":["WIS"]},"Prophesied":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Your fate is foretold: while the prophecy plays out, the GM decides your rolls.","full":"A fortune-teller or a great prophecy has fixed one moment of your future. Choose the prophecy and share it with the GM. When it comes true, you do not roll attack rolls, ability checks or saving throws during the prophesied events. The GM decides those results for you.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Proto-Man":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Advantage against fear and a free Hit Die on each Short Rest, once per Long Rest.","full":"**Brave.** You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the frightened condition on you.\n**Primal Recovery.** When you take a Short Rest you can regain 1 Hit Die and spend it right away. A Long Rest restores this use.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Psionic":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Read emotions, invisible Mage Hand, then Unseen Servant and Levitate once each per Long Rest.","full":"**Empathy.** As an action, probe the surface emotions of a creature within 30 feet that you see and that has Intelligence 3 or higher. You learn its emotional state and, at the GM's discretion, one of its Bonds.\n**Psionics.** You know the Mage Hand cantrip, and the hand is invisible when you cast it this way. At level 3 you can cast Unseen Servant once with this trait, and at level 5 Levitate once. A Long Rest restores each. You can also cast them with slots of the right level. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma as the spellcasting ability when you take the feat.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Reptiloid":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Replace an attack with a 30 ft acid spit, 1d10 acid scaling with level, Proficiency Bonus uses per Long Rest.","full":"**Acid Spit.** When you take the Attack action you can replace one attack with a lob of acid. It is a ranged attack with range 30 feet, you are proficient with it, and you add your Dexterity modifier to its attack and damage rolls. A hit deals 1d10 acid damage, rising to 2d10 at level 5, 3d10 at level 11 and 4d10 at level 17. You can use it a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and a Long Rest restores all uses.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Roguean":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Darkvision 60 ft, Cold resistance, and tolerance of -100 to 300 degrees Fahrenheit.","full":"**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 60 feet as if bright, and in darkness as if dim. You see only shades of gray in darkness.\n**Cold Resistance.** You have Resistance to Cold damage.\n**Extremophile.** You can endure temperatures from -100 to 300 degrees Fahrenheit.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Cold"],"senses":[["Darkvision",60,""]]}},"Secret":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Pick one falsehood about yourself. You never need a Deception check to maintain it.","full":"Choose one falsehood about yourself and practice it until you can recite it perfectly. It can be one lie or a whole false history. You never need a Deception check to maintain this falsehood.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Showman (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Performance proficiency or expertise, and a bonus equal to your audience size (up to Charisma modifier) three times per Long Rest.","full":"You gain proficiency in Performance. If you already have it, you add double your Proficiency Bonus to it instead.\nWhen a non-hostile audience watches you fight, once per turn you can add a bonus to an ability check or attack roll equal to the number of onlookers, up to your Charisma modifier. You can do this three times, and a Long Rest restores all uses.","asi":["CHA"],"fx":{"skills":["Performance"]}},"Soul Twin":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Two bodies, one soul: shared actions, separate hit points, spells and effects mostly hit both.","full":"You and your twin are identical twins who share one soul, a single character with two bodies you control.\n**Actions.** The twins share one action, bonus action and reaction per turn. If you take Dash, Disengage, Dodge, Help, Hide, Ready or Search, both twins gain the benefit.\n**Attacks.** When one twin attacks with the Attack action, the other can attack as a bonus action, adding no ability modifier to damage unless it is negative. With several attacks you can split them between the twins.\n**Hit Points.** Each twin has its own hit points. At 1st level each has the hit points of a normal character of your class. At each level each twin gains your Constitution modifier plus half the Hit Die (rounded up), or 2, 3, 3 or 4 for d6, d8, d10 or d12 average. You spend Hit Dice separately for each twin.\n**Spellcasting.** You can concentrate on one spell at a time, and one twin concentrating is enough. Either twin can supply components, and a spell can originate from either twin.\n**Magical Effects.** A spell or ability that affects one twin affects both, unless it deals with hit points or the twins are over 100 feet apart. Then it affects each separately.\n**Conditions.** A condition affects only the twin it was put on.\n**Death.** When one twin starts making death saves, the other is incapacitated with halved Speed. If one twin dies, the other dies 24 hours later unless the partner returns to life.\n**Empathic Link.** On the same plane, the twins sense each other's emotions and know when the other takes damage.\nAs a rule of thumb, effects that heal, harm or grab affect one twin, and effects that charm, curse, enchant or protect affect both. The GM rules unclear cases. This is an advanced option, not for new players or those who control many creatures.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Spellblade (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"One martial melee weapon, elemental damage swaps on melee hits, two blade cantrips, and Shield once per Long Rest.","full":"You gain proficiency with one martial melee weapon. When you deal bludgeoning, piercing or slashing damage with a melee weapon, you can change it to acid, cold, fire or lightning damage. You learn two cantrips from Arc Blade, Burning Blade, Caustic Blade and Frigid Blade, using Intelligence. You can cast Shield once with no slot, and a Long Rest restores that."},"Stheno":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Replace an attack with a 60 ft gaze: Constitution save or incapacitated with Speed 0, Proficiency Bonus uses.","full":"**Immobilizing Gaze.** When you take the Attack action you can replace one attack with this gaze. Pick a creature within 60 feet that can see you. It makes a Constitution save (DC 8 + your Constitution modifier + your Proficiency Bonus). A creature immune to being restrained succeeds automatically. On a failed save it is incapacitated and its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn. You can use it a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and a Long Rest restores all uses.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Stoneborn":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"+1 AC, Advantage against being knocked prone or moved, and sense gems and metals in stone.","full":"**Stony Skin.** You have a +1 bonus to AC.\n**Sure-Footed.** You have Advantage on ability checks and saves to resist being knocked prone or moved against your will.\n**Oresight.** With a hand on natural stone and an action to focus, you feel natural gems or metals within 100 feet.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Stony Skin: +1 bonus to AC"]]}},"Tauran":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Horns for 1d6 piercing unarmed strikes, always know north, and +10 ft Speed on straight-line turns.","full":"**Horns.** Your horns make unarmed strikes that deal 1d6 + your Strength modifier piercing damage.\n**Labyrinthine Recall.** You always know which way is north and have Advantage on Wisdom (Survival) checks to navigate or track.\n**Rush.** On any turn in which you move only in a straight line, your Speed rises by 10 feet.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Traveler":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Disadvantage on History checks about this land, and you can share simple ideas by gesture.","full":"You come from a place so far away that you may never return, perhaps another plane, another time or the far side of the ocean. You know little of this land, its history and its people, and they know little of you. You have Disadvantage on Intelligence (History) checks about the history or customs of this land. You can communicate simple ideas through gestures to any creature that understands at least one language.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Troll-Blooded":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Regain 1 hit point per minute while at one quarter of your hit points or less (not at 0).","full":"**Troll Regeneration.** You regain 1 hit point each minute while you have no more than one quarter of your hit points (rounded down). You cannot use this trait at 0 hit points.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Two-Headed":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Advantage against blinded, charmed, deafened and frightened, and you stay conscious during a Long Rest.","full":"**Two-Heads.** You have Advantage on saves to avoid or end the blinded, charmed, deafened and frightened conditions on you.\n**Wakeful.** One head is always awake, so you remain conscious during a Long Rest.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Two-Heads: Advantage on saves against being blinded, charmed, deafened or frightened"]]}},"Undead":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"No need to eat, drink, sleep or breathe. Advantage on poison saves and Poison resistance.","full":"You are caught between death and life, a revenant, a lich or something unique born of a curse or accident. You do not need to eat, drink, sleep or breathe. You still spend 8 hours in light activity, such as keeping watch, to gain the benefit of a Long Rest. You have Advantage on saves against poison and Resistance to Poison damage. Your type is Humanoid, but spells and effects that target undead also affect you.","pre":"Character creation only","fx":{"res":["Poison"],"notes":[["Note","Undead: Advantage on saves against poison. You do not need to eat, drink, sleep or breathe"]]}},"Upcaster":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Combine two slots of one level into a slot one level higher and cast a known or prepared spell with it.","full":"You can spend two spell slots of the same level to create one slot a level higher and immediately cast a spell you know or have prepared with it.","pre":"Spellcasting"},"Upper Limb Disability":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Pick a Disadvantage for heavy or for finesse and ranged weapons, and gain Advantage on readied weapon attacks.","full":"Injury, illness or birth means you cannot use your arms as others do. The cause might be paralysis, an amputated arm or hand, poor manual dexterity, arthritis or chronic pain. Even without an arm or hand you can fight with two weapons or a weapon and shield through prosthetics or a mechanical or magical aid.\nChoose one trait that fits your disability: Disadvantage on attack rolls with heavy weapons and on Strength checks that need your hands, or Disadvantage on attack rolls with finesse and ranged weapons and on Dexterity checks that need your hands.\nYou also have Advantage on weapon attacks you prepare with the Ready action.\nIf your limb is ever restored, such as by Regenerate, you lose this feat. Talk with your GM about whether that fits your character.","pre":"Character creation only"},"Windswept":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Lightning resistance, Message, then Feather Fall and Gust of Wind once each per Long Rest.","full":"**Lightning Resistance.** You have Resistance to Lightning damage.\n**Zephyr Magic.** You know the Message cantrip. At level 3 you can cast Feather Fall once with this trait, and at level 5 Gust of Wind once, with no material component. A Long Rest restores each. You can also cast them with slots of the right level. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma as the spellcasting ability when you take the feat.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Lightning"]}},"Winged":{"cat":"G","hb":"VSS14","d":"Flying Speed equal to your walking Speed, unusable in medium or heavy armor.","full":"**Flight.** Your wings give you a flying Speed equal to your walking Speed. You cannot use it while wearing medium or heavy armor.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"mv":{"fly":"speed"}}},"Crippling":{"cat":"F","hb":"VSS14","d":"When you hit a creature with a Melee weapon attack, its Speed drops by 10 feet (minimum 0) until the end of its next turn, and it cannot Dash until then.","full":"When you hit a creature with a Melee weapon attack, its Speed drops by 10 feet, to a minimum of 0, until the end of its next turn. It also cannot take the Dash action until the end of that turn.","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Crippling: a Melee weapon hit cuts the target's Speed by 10 ft and blocks its Dash until the end of its next turn"]]}},"Titan Fighting":{"cat":"F","hb":"VSS14","d":"+2 bonus to Melee weapon attack rolls against Large or larger creatures.","full":"You have a +2 bonus to Melee weapon attack rolls you make against creatures that are Large or larger.","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Titan Fighting: +2 to Melee weapon attack rolls against Large or larger creatures"]]}}};
